{
  "comment": [
    "UNION ALL phase 3: a compound as a row source and as an ordinary CTE body.",
    "",
    "Nine classes. They attack what phase 3 introduced — the source term, the",
    "output names a compound provides, the every-column-named rule, and the",
    "non-recursive CTE path — plus the three compiler rules that phase 3 is the",
    "first thing to make reachable from the public API: nested parenthesisation,",
    "global placeholder numbering, and the parameters an enclosing statement had",
    "already collected.",
    "",
    "Kept apart from manifest.json, uuidmanifest.json and unionmanifest.json, whose",
    "accounting is closed. UNION ALL is not frozen and this is not the UNION",
    "manifest; it is the focused set for one integration slice.",
    "",
    "Every killer runs in the root module and needs no database. The server-side",
    "proof is in internal/gendemo/m16_unionsource_test.go, which is not part of",
    "this campaign."
  ],
  "evidence_commit": "ab3e1df",
  "evidence_commit_note": [
    "ab3e1df is the revision every UNION ALL class was last applied to and run at, in a",
    "worktree checked out at exactly that commit, with the manifests read and written",
    "outside it so the tree stayed clean between classes. It is kept reachable as",
    "archive/m16-union-mutation-evidence.",
    "",
    "The five UNION ALL campaigns were rerun together at one revision after `mutate",
    "anchors` found four anchors that later phases had silently invalidated by editing",
    "the code they quote. An anchor that no longer matches makes its class look like a",
    "survivor, so the campaigns were pinned to revisions where they no longer ran.",
    "They run again, and three harness controls were active: anchors still quote their",
    "code, every site names the function its anchor is inside, and each semantic probe",
    "survives every mutation in another function."
  ],
  "not_expressible": [
    {
      "id": "P3-X1",
      "name": "A foreign implementation of the sealed source interface is accepted",
      "why": [
        "SourceTerm is closed by an unexported method, so a type outside the",
        "package cannot satisfy it and no code runs to decide whether it does.",
        "There is nothing to mutate: the rule is the Go compiler's. It is asserted",
        "instead by the compile-fail case \"a type outside the package claiming to",
        "be a row source\", which compiles a whole program and requires it to fail."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "P3-X2",
      "name": "Recursive CTE validation accepts a compound without validating it",
      "why": [
        "recursiveCTE takes a Term and passes two *expr.Select values to",
        "ValidateRecursive. A compound is not a Select and there is no assignment",
        "that would make it one, so the defect cannot be written. It is asserted by",
        "the compile-fail case \"a set operation as a recursive CTE's anchor\".",
        "",
        "Deleting the ValidateRecursive call would be a real mutation, but it is a",
        "mutation of the recursive path, which this phase deliberately did not",
        "touch. It belongs to whichever phase takes recursive CTEs on."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "classes": [
